IMPORT prelude
IMPORT properties

-- MUTANT of d3-atomic.l4: a bought dinner can be cancelled. P4 MUST FAIL.
--
-- P4 says a bought dinner stays bought, and in D3 it holds by
-- construction: nothing ever takes a dinner back. A check that cannot fail
-- proves nothing about the checker, so this mutant adds one act and the
-- property must go red on it (REGULATIVE-LOWERING-SPEC.md section 6.3).
--
-- The whole difference from d3-atomic.l4, apart from comments, section
-- names and the traces:
--   * the act `Alice cancels the dinner`, enabled once Alice has bought
--     and one dinner is bought;
--   * its effect, a COMMIT to `dinners cancelled`, which takes the count of
--     dinners from 1 back to 0.
-- properties.l4 here is a link to ../properties.l4: an IMPORT cannot reach
-- a parent directory.

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `ledger records Bob's purchase`            -- BobBuys
    `Messages delivers the message`            -- Deliver
    `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`    -- CheckBought
    `Alice is done`                            -- Done
    `Alice buys dinner`                        -- BuyChecked if answered, NoAnswer if not
        HAS `ledger answered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Alice cancels the dinner`                 -- Cancel (THE MUTATION)

`closing` MEANS 75600

§ `D3 with a cancel: the guards`

GIVEN act IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the brief allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase`         THEN `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
    WHEN `Messages delivers the message`         THEN (RECALL Messages's `message`) EQUALS JUST `in transit`
    WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS planning
    WHEN `Alice is done`                         THEN `Alice has bought or stopped` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
    WHEN `Alice buys dinner` answered            THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS checked
    WHEN `Alice cancels the dinner`              THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS bought
                                                      AND `one dinner is bought` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinners bought`) (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinners cancelled`)

§ `D3 with a cancel: the arrangement`

-- The arrangement opens with dinner unbought: the ledger's first record.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the arrangement` MEANS
    COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
    HENCE `the evening`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the evening` MEANS
    PARTY World
    MAY   act PROVIDED `the brief allows` act
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE CONSIDER act
          WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase` THEN
              COMMIT `dinner status record` IS taken
              HENCE RECORD Messages's `message` IS `in transit`
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Messages delivers the message` THEN
              RECORD Messages's `message` IS delivered
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `belief` IS taken
              HENCE `Alice stops unless she has bought` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
          WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN
              RECORD Alice's `belief` IS `the ledger's status` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS checked
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice is done` THEN `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice buys dinner` answered THEN
              IF NOT answered
              THEN `the evening`
              ELSE `the ledger answers the purchase` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
          WHEN `Alice cancels the dinner` THEN
              COMMIT `dinners cancelled` IS `dinner for two`
              HENCE `the evening`
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- The ledger's answer, in one step: accept and record the purchase if
-- dinner is open at this instant, refuse it if Bob's purchase has taken it.
GIVEN `dinner status record` IS A LIST OF Status
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the ledger answers the purchase` MEANS
    IF `the ledger is open` `dinner status record`
    THEN COMMIT `dinners bought` IS `dinner for two`
         HENCE COMMIT `open at acceptance` IS `the ledger is open` `dinner status record`
         HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS bought
         HENCE `the evening`
    ELSE RECORD Alice's `belief` IS taken
         HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
         HENCE `the evening`

-- The message stops Alice if she is still on her way to buying.
GIVEN plan IS A MAYBE Plan
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice stops unless she has bought` MEANS
    IF `Alice has bought or stopped` plan
    THEN `the evening`
    ELSE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
         HENCE `the evening`

§ `D3 with a cancel: the traces`

-- Sequence B, then Alice cancels at 18:09. Official record: opened, dinner
-- for two, open at acceptance TRUE, taken, and then dinners cancelled. The
-- count of dinners goes from 1 to 0: P4 fails.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES (`Alice buys dinner` TRUE)              AT 65130
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `Alice cancels the dinner`              AT 65340
    PARTY World DOES `Alice cancels the dinner`              AT 65350
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)
